# Pipeline Order

All analyses were performed using GRCh38 coordinates.

Ancestry-specific LD reference panels were generated using 1000 Genomes Project reference data.

## Required Input Data

- COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative (HGI) Release 7 summary statistics
- SLE GWAS summary statistics
- eQTLGen SMR-formatted cis-eQTL data
- chain file
- 1000 Genomes Project GRCh38 reference panel
- FASTA file

# Analysis Workflow

bash 01_extract_loci.sh - extracts lead SNP and locus files used throughout the analysis.
Rscript 02_extract_gwas_loci.R - Extracts GWAS variants within the specified genomic windows
bash 03_extracting_eQTLgen_region.sh - Extracts matching cis-eQTL regions from eQTLGen SMR-formatted data.
Rscript 04_liftover_eqtl.R - Converts genomic coordinates to GRCh38 where required. 
Rscript 05_align_gwas_eqtl.R - Aligns alleles and matches variants between GWAS and eQTL datasets and saves SNP list and ref allele list for LD matrix.
bash 06_create_ld_reference.sh - Generates EUR and EAS LD reference datasets from 1000 Genomes Project samples. 
bash 07_compute_ld.sh - Computes ancestry-specific LD matrices for each locus. 
Rscript 08_coloc_analysis.R - Performs Bayesian colocalisation analysis between GWAS and eQTL signals and provides overview of any loc with pph4 >0.5.
Rscript 09_coloc_susie.R - Performs SuSiE-based fine-mapping and colocalisation analysis.

### Output

Main outputs include:
GWAS summary statistics
LD matrices
coloc posterior probabilities
SuSiE credible sets
lead SNP summary tables
ancestry-specific colocalisation results
